1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,481
Most freelance scope problems do not start with bad intent.

2
00:00:03,481 --> 00:00:08,095
They start when the brief, the decision, and the proof live in different places.

3
00:00:08,095 --> 00:00:09,591
This is Delividence.

4
00:00:09,591 --> 00:00:15,163
The owner starts with the real landing page, signs in, and creates a record from a plain client brief.

5
00:00:15,163 --> 00:00:23,528
Gemini turns that brief into working project state: source material, acceptance criteria, and an activity trail that shows what the agent did.

6
00:00:23,528 --> 00:00:26,787
The important thing is that this is not just a chat answer.

7
00:00:26,787 --> 00:00:30,373
It becomes a shared ledger the project can actually run on.

8
00:00:30,373 --> 00:00:34,275
The client receives a no-account portal and confirms the first baseline.

9
00:00:34,275 --> 00:00:38,703
Now both sides know exactly what version one means before delivery starts.

10
00:00:38,703 --> 00:00:40,303
Here is the guardrail.

11
00:00:40,303 --> 00:00:50,327
When the client asks for three vertical TikTok visuals, Delividence checks the request against the accepted baseline, cites the original deliverable, and recommends a change request.

12
00:00:50,327 --> 00:00:54,314
A human can confirm the classification before the scope changes.

13
00:00:54,314 --> 00:01:00,689
Then the owner proposes the new criterion, attaches proof, and sends the delivery review back to the client.

14
00:01:00,689 --> 00:01:07,418
The client can accept one item and request changes on another, so review becomes precise instead of emotional.

15
00:01:07,418 --> 00:01:18,574
The main app also has the operational views judges should expect: Records for every project, Sources for what was used, Review for current decisions, Activity for the audit trail, and Policies for default review rules.

16
00:01:18,574 --> 00:01:32,546
The backend is running on Google Cloud Run: a public API service, a private worker service, Pub/Sub for asynchronous jobs, Firestore for durable state, Firebase Auth for secure sessions, and Gemini for extraction and scope classification.

17
00:01:32,546 --> 00:01:41,985
The value is simple: Delividence removes the manual chasing around scope, evidence, and approvals, while keeping a human in control of the decisions that matter.

